From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:44:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 210/219] feat: real skinning of characters in the software
 triangle ray tracer (decision 07, stage 3B)

Characters used to reflect in their bind pose: CE 5.7.1 skins on the GPU or, in the vertex
animation fallback, into a write only discard mapped vertex buffer, and the skin -> skeleton
bone remap table never left CryAnimation. The data was all there; only the interface was
missing.

CryAnimation
- IAttachmentSkin::GetSkinnedVertexCount(lod) and GetSkinnedVertices(lod, pos, norm, tang,
  capacity), appended at the VERY END of the interface so the vtable only grows at the back and
  every slot an already compiled module resolved keeps its index. All buffers are owned and
  sized by the caller - no STL crosses the module boundary.
- CAttachmentSKIN implements them by driving the very same VertexCommandSkin the software
  skinning path compiles into its command buffer, with the master character's current
  SSkinningData::pBoneQuatsS and this attachment's m_arrRemapTable, over the CSoftwareMesh
  CModelMesh keeps (or lazily builds) for that LOD. Same dual quaternions, same blend, same
  tangent frame, and the render mesh offset is included exactly as the vertex shader adds it.
  Returns 0 when the character has no skinning data yet, so the caller can keep an older pose.
- CAttachmentVCLOTH returns 0: cloth is simulated, not skinned, and has no CPU side result.
- ca_RTSkinSelfTest: synthetic two bone skin (three quads - identity, 90 deg X, 50-50 blend)
  through the same function, compared against the analytic transform.

Cry3DEngine
- The cached per object BVH now optionally keeps the three SOURCE vertex indices per triangle,
  permuted with the triangles, so a deformed copy can be looked up per vertex.
- RTUpdateDynamic CPU skins the kept characters nearest first under e_svoTI_RT_SkinMaxTris
  (new cvar, 30000 triangles per frame), swaps the skinned positions and normals in before the
  instance matrix and refits the cached topology onto them - no rebuild. A skinned instance
  takes its world box and quantisation bounds from the refit's exact root box, because an
  animated pose leaves the bind pose box.
- Per attachment skinned vertex cache, so an attachment whose skinning data is not ready keeps
  its last good pose instead of snapping back to the bind pose mid animation.
- RT dyn: stats line gains "skinned N chars, T K verts, S stale, X.XX ms".

CryAnimation and Cry3DEngine both build Profile with 0 errors / 0 warnings. The engine was not
run and nothing was deployed.

