+	//! Number of vertices GetSkinnedVertices() writes for this LOD, 0 if the LOD has no usable mesh.
+	//! Cheap: it does not touch the skinning data and does not build any CPU side buffer.
+	virtual uint32 GetSkinnedVertexCount(uint32 lod) = 0;
+
+	//! CPU skins this attachment's LOD with the CURRENT frame's bone transforms, through the very same
+	//! dual quaternion path the engine's own software skinning uses, so the result matches what the GPU
+	//! computes for the same pose.
+	//!
+	//! Every buffer is owned and sized by the CALLER - no STL container ever crosses the module
+	//! boundary. pPositions is mandatory; pNormals and pTangents may be null when they are not needed
+	//! (pTangents is xyz = tangent, w = the +-1 bitangent sign). capacity is the number of VERTICES the
+	//! buffers hold and must be at least GetSkinnedVertexCount(lod).
+	//!
+	//! eturn the number of vertices written, or 0 when nothing could be produced - in particular when
+	//! the character has no skinning data yet this frame. The caller should then keep whatever it
+	//! computed on a previous frame rather than fall back to the bind pose mid animation.
+	virtual uint32 GetSkinnedVertices(uint32 lod, Vec3* pPositions, Vec3* pNormals, Vec4* pTangents, uint32 capacity) = 0;
